                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "982f6e9c-80aa-4b84-bf39-eb64cc3a97c7",
                                                "sense_id": "46906557-5b69-3bbd-84bc-392c5e78cbc4",
                                                "text": "It is hard to get purchase on a nail without a pry bar or hammer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9706d1f-8401-4525-8de3-5592aedc5d8c",
                                                "sense_id": "46906557-5b69-3bbd-84bc-392c5e78cbc4",
                                                "text": "The problem is that the model of individual responsibility assumed by most versions of ethics have little purchase on the behavior of Capital or corporations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39d6738a-09d7-3879-9014-bdc150cdbf0c",
                                        "entry_id": "4cf36d3f-10b2-386e-ac84-c406a8c9d0d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The apparatus, tackle or device by which such mechanical advantage is gained and (in nautical terminology) the ratio of such a device, like a pulley, or block and tackle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0c2331e-d3e1-4db4-bb10-328249df4ea0",
                                                "sense_id": "39d6738a-09d7-3879-9014-bdc150cdbf0c",
                                                "text": "He describes the operation thus: \"The heavy ram employed to impart the finishing strokes, hoisted up with double purchase and snail's pace to the summit of the Piling Engine, and then falling down like a thunderbolt on the head of the devoted timber, driving it perhaps a single half inch in to the stratum below, is well calculated to put to the test the virtue of patience, while it illustrates the old adage of—slow and sure.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67ad0c50-b7bc-3942-9c64-a12acda3a040",
                                        "entry_id": "4cf36d3f-10b2-386e-ac84-c406a8c9d0d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The amount of hold one has from an individual foothold or ledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "087b2ab6-9233-4ac1-9505-cabceda00cb5",
                                                "sense_id": "67ad0c50-b7bc-3942-9c64-a12acda3a040",
                                                "text": "At first, he was climbing down, testing for purchase with his feet. But soon, as the entire section of ground rotated, he was lifted into the air, and up and down flipped around."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a50a54f-5217-3c74-a73e-0c8ed61dab2b",
                                        "entry_id": "4cf36d3f-10b2-386e-ac84-c406a8c9d0d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Acquisition of lands or tenements by means other than descent or inheritance, namely, by one's own act or agreement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5048bf84-fcc2-494e-9747-02b967ecb397",
                                                "sense_id": "0a50a54f-5217-3c74-a73e-0c8ed61dab2b",
                                                "text": "The difference […]between the acquisition of an estate by descent and by purchase"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "purchase",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0044a17e-398f-34cc-b232-6b6d1da59889",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To buy, obtain by payment of a price in money or its equivalent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "957f6080-377b-43b0-8a75-79e0123249d1",
                                                "sense_id": "0044a17e-398f-34cc-b232-6b6d1da59889",
                                                "text": "to purchase land, to purchase a house"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a892030-cec9-3b94-aa9b-351dff72ed91",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pursue and obtain; to acquire by seeking; to gain, obtain, or acquire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b7433aa-abf2-46f8-b16f-4c880f773ba2",
                                                "sense_id": "7a892030-cec9-3b94-aa9b-351dff72ed91",
                                                "text": "that loves the thing he cannot purchase"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "458b0794-003e-4819-bd45-13f198e65616",
                                                "sense_id": "7a892030-cec9-3b94-aa9b-351dff72ed91",
                                                "text": "They [the English] are all on fire / To purchaſe from the Spaniard. If their Carracks / Come deeply laden, vvee ſhall tugge vvith them / For golden ſpoile."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6af8e76f-187f-429b-9c6e-6ee05bb3111f",
                                                "sense_id": "7a892030-cec9-3b94-aa9b-351dff72ed91",
                                                "text": "Your accent is something finer than you could purchase in so removed a dwelling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bc5b810-c2d8-4436-9378-8d2a396a4297",
                                                "sense_id": "7a892030-cec9-3b94-aa9b-351dff72ed91",
                                                "text": "His faults […] hereditary / Rather than purchased."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc105667-4a6f-35d7-9561-95f8cd61ee61",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To obtain by any outlay, as of labor, danger, or sacrifice, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dff1374b-62e4-440b-bc0a-083ab4333fd7",
                                                "sense_id": "bc105667-4a6f-35d7-9561-95f8cd61ee61",
                                                "text": "to purchase favor with flattery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b337895c-e647-46ea-9fdb-5baa67ad724c",
                                                "sense_id": "bc105667-4a6f-35d7-9561-95f8cd61ee61",
                                                "text": "One poor retiring minute […] / Would purchase thee a thousand thousand friends."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c483e174-2d7f-397f-a319-3df67ec1faee",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To expiate by a fine or forfeit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "820d0829-8b40-4e49-ac44-82cbea9f3ca5",
                                                "sense_id": "c483e174-2d7f-397f-a319-3df67ec1faee",
                                                "text": "Not tears nor prayers shall purchase out abuses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3506927-4e29-33fb-8997-52b450dcb0c6",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To apply to (anything) a device for obtaining a mechanical advantage; to get a purchase upon, or apply a purchase to; to raise or move by mechanical means."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59b1854c-2f4d-4aa4-844e-d2fc1e652827",
                                                "sense_id": "a3506927-4e29-33fb-8997-52b450dcb0c6",
                                                "text": "to purchase a cannon"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c43d79d0-d348-3adb-81af-95ecc70ef9a3",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put forth effort to obtain anything; to strive; to exert oneself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8d592e1-88aa-4737-9cd0-14a23ee83340",
                                                "sense_id": "c43d79d0-d348-3adb-81af-95ecc70ef9a3",
                                                "text": "1523–1525, John Bourchier, 2nd Baron Berners, Froissart's Chronicles\nDuke John of Brabant purchased greatly that the Earl of Flanders should have his daughter in marriage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee6131c3-a731-37a2-9c82-ea81277d46ed",
                                        "entry_id": "b32b2bf4-4984-3295-a17b-94f9df16965c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To constitute the buying power for a purchase, have a trading value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3f3086a-e7b4-4c1a-b7da-8858ad04c559",
                                                "sense_id": "ee6131c3-a731-37a2-9c82-ea81277d46ed",
                                                "text": "Many aristocratic refugees' portable treasures purchased their safe passage and comfortable exile during the revolution."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
